- `actor(a_default, "Default", [...])`: Assigns process responsibilities to a "Default" actor instead of the source-specified participant ("For buyers, the process begins..."). (SMC7)
- `label(n5, c1, "After selecting preferred copy")` and `label(n8, c1, "After selecting preferred copy")`: Incorrectly assert a selection event; `n5` and `n8` correspond to viewing steps ("see a list of new copies", "view a list of new copies from book details"), whereas the source explicitly ties selection actions to other paths ("proceed to select a copy", "select their preferred copy to complete the process"). (SMC1, SMC2)
- `defines(v1, "...", {})` and `defines(v2, "...", {})`: Specify empty value ranges `{}` for decision variables, omitting the concrete alternatives explicitly detailed in the source ("view the book details", "see a list of new copies", "view a list of used copies"). (SMC6)

